    [CI] Remove internal cache-service references from test workflows (#17687)
    
    ## What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    This is the test-pipeline counterpart of #17100. It removes all internal
    cache-service references from the test workflows, so tests use public
    sources only (the cluster relies on a squid proxy cache for public
    sources; the internal nginx-pypi-cache mirror service is no longer
    needed).
    
    Changes (9 workflow files + 1 installation doctest script):
    
    - **pr_test.yaml**: drop the internal `UV_INDEX_URL` env in the
    pre-commit install step
    - **_selected_tests.yaml / _selected_tests_upstream.yaml /
    schedule_main2main.yaml / schedule_e2e_upstream_test.yaml**: drop the
    internal `UV_INDEX_URL` and `UV_INSECURE_HOST` env vars, strip the
    internal `cache-service.../whl/cpu/` entry from `UV_EXTRA_INDEX_URL`,
    remove the APT source rewriting (`cache-service :8081`) and the `pip
    config set` lines; rename the "Config mirrors" steps to "Install
    packages"
    - **_e2e_nightly_single_node.yaml / _560t.yaml / _models.yaml**
    (Nightly/Weekly A2, A3, A3-560T, A5, 310P): same cleanup for the
    `UV_INDEX_URL` env block and the APT/pip-config lines in "Check npu and
    CANN info"
    - **_build_csrc_cache.yaml**: same cleanup for both the ubuntu (APT) and
    openeuler (YUM) paths
    - **tests/e2e/doctests/002-installation-test.sh**: drop `CACHE_HOST`,
    the APT/YUM mirror rewriting helper, and `PIP_TRUSTED_HOST` /
    `UV_INSECURE_HOST`; keep the retry/timeout settings and the git clone
    retry wrapper
    
    All public sources are kept unchanged: Huawei Cloud Ascend repo
    (`repo.huaweicloud.com/ascend/repos/pypi`), PyTorch CPU wheels,
    `triton-ascend.osinfra.cn`, and the Huawei Cloud Go proxy.
    
    Affected runners (one-to-one map): `linux-amd64-cpu-8-hk` (pre-commit /
    recommend-tests / select-tests / cpu-ut), `linux-aarch64-a2b3-1`
    (upstream e2e), `linux-aarch64-a3-16-sh-001` (main2main),
    `linux-amd64-cpu-4-hk` (resolve-tag), all nightly/weekly NPU machines
    from `nightly_config.yaml` (`linux-aarch64-a2b3-N`,
    `linux-aarch64-a3-800i-N`, `linux-aarch64-a5-8`,
    `linux-aarch64-310p-N`), and `linux-arm64-cpu-16` (csrc cache builds).
    
    Image build files are intentionally NOT touched here — they are covered
    by #17100.
    
    ## Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This only affects the CI test pipeline's internal configuration;
    test coverage and behavior are unchanged.
    
    ## How was this patch tested?
    
    - Repo-wide grep verification: no remaining `cache-service` references
    anywhere in the repo (only `_schedule_image_build.yaml` /
    `_nightly_image_build.yaml` remain, which belong to #17100)
    - All 9 modified workflow files pass YAML syntax validation
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: chenqi49 <479148871@qq.com>

